{"name":"Dark Sky","hex":"#909989","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dark Skies (1929 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Dark Skies is a 1929 American pre-Code crime drama film directed by Harry S. Webb and starring Shirley Mason, Wallace MacDonald and William V. Mong. Made by the Poverty Row studio Biltmore Productions it was an early low-budget talkie, set in a California coastal community. It featured the hit song \"Juanita\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Skies_(1929_film)"},{"title":"Dark Skies (2013 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Dark Skies is a 2013 science fiction horror film written and directed by Scott Stewart, produced by Jason Blum under his Blumhouse Productions banner, and starring Keri Russell, Josh Hamilton, Dakota Goyo and J. K. Simmons."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7f/Dark_Skies_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Skies_(2013_film)"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg/500px-Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg/1280px-Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg/500px-Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cirriform clouds and a quarter Moon in the blue daytime sky over Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASky_over_Munich_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg/500px-Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg/1280px-Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg/500px-Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.